input.body:
If reading the result fails partway (connection reset, context canceled), `rows.Next()` returns false and this falls through to `ErrNoLane`. The quote handler turns that into a 404 "no lane for this route" (internal/server/quotes.go:40), so a database error reaches the customer as a missing lane and never shows up in the error log. `rows.Err()` is never checked either.

The query has `LIMIT 1`, so `QueryRowContext` is simpler and keeps the two cases apart (with the SQL moved into a `laneQuery` const):

```go
var l Lane
err := s.db.QueryRowContext(ctx, laneQuery, origin, dest, zip3State[origin], zip3State[dest]).
	Scan(&l.ID, &l.OriginKey, &l.DestKey, &l.Miles, &l.RatePerMile)
if errors.Is(err, sql.ErrNoRows) {
	return Lane{}, ErrNoLane
}
if err != nil {
	return Lane{}, fmt.Errorf("query lanes: %w", err)
}
return l, nil
```

